    "abstract": "A square-tiled surface (STS) is a branched cover of the standard square torus with branching\nover exactly one point. In this paper we consider a randomizing model for STSs and general-\nizations to branched covers of other simple translation surfaces which we call polygon-tiled\nsurfaces. We obtain a local central limit theorem for the genus and subsequently obtain\nthat the distribution of the genus is asymptotically normal. We also study holonomy vec-\ntors (Euclidean displacement vectors between cone points) on a random STS. We show that\nasymptotically almost surely the set of holonomy vectors of a random STS contains the set\nof primitive vectors of Z2 and with probability approaching 1/e, these sets are equal.",
    "abstract_method": "pdftotext-2pages",
    "abstract_search_scope": "first2pages"
  },
